{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const {\n  fetchNextPage,\n  fetchPreviousPage,\n  hasNextPage,\n  hasPreviousPage,\n  isFetchingNextPage,\n  isFetchingPreviousPage,\n  ...result\n} = useInfiniteQuery({\n  queryKey,\n  queryFn: ({ pageParam = 1 }) => fetchPage(pageParam),\n  ...options,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage, allPages) => lastPage.nextCursor,\n  getPreviousPageParam: (firstPage, allPages) => firstPage.prevCursor,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The options for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useInfiniteQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" are identical to the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../../framework/react/reference/useQuery","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" hook"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the addition of the following:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn: (context: QueryFunctionContext) => Promise<TData>"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required, but only if no default query function has been defined"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../../framework/react/guides/default-query-function","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultQueryFn"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function that the query will use to request data."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Receives a "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../../framework/react/guides/query-functions#queryfunctioncontext","children":[{"type":"text","value":"QueryFunctionContext"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Must return a promise that will either resolve data or throw an error."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Make sure you return the data "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"and"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" if needed for use in the props below."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getNextPageParam: (lastPage, allPages) => unknown | undefined"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When new data is received for this query, this function receives both the last page of the infinite list of data and the full array of all pages."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It should return a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"single variable"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that will be passed as the last optional parameter to your query function."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" to indicate there is no next page available."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreviousPageParam: (firstPage, allPages) => unknown | undefined"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When new data is received for this query, this function receives both the first page of the infinite list of data and the full array of all pages."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It should return a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"single variable"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that will be passed as the last optional parameter to your query function."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" to indicate there is no previous page available."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned properties for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useInfiniteQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" are identical to the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../../framework/react/reference/useQuery","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" hook"}]},{"type":"text","value":", with the addition of the following and a small difference in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRefetching"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data.pages: TData[]"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array containing all pages."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data.pageParams: unknown[]"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array containing all page params."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFetchingNextPage: boolean"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Will be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" while fetching the next page with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFetchingPreviousPage: boolean"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Will be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" while fetching the previous page with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchPreviousPage"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchNextPage: (options?: FetchNextPageOptions) => Promise<UseInfiniteQueryResult>"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function allows you to fetch the next \"page\" of results."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.pageParam: unknown"},{"type":"text","value":" allows you to manually specify a page param instead of using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getNextPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.cancelRefetch: boolean"},{"type":"text","value":" if set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":" repeatedly will invoke "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchPage"},{"type":"text","value":" every time, whether the previous\ninvocation has resolved or not. Also, the result from previous invocations will be ignored. If set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":", calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":"\nrepeatedly won't have any effect until the first invocation has resolved. Default is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchPreviousPage: (options?: FetchPreviousPageOptions) => Promise<UseInfiniteQueryResult>"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function allows you to fetch the previous \"page\" of results."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.pageParam: unknown"},{"type":"text","value":" allows you to manually specify a page param instead of using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreviousPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.cancelRefetch: boolean"},{"type":"text","value":" same as for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasNextPage: boolean"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This will be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if there is a next page to be fetched (known via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getNextPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" option)."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasPreviousPage: boolean"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This will be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if there is a previous page to be fetched (known via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreviousPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" option)."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRefetching: boolean"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" whenever a background refetch is in-flight, which "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"does not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" include initial "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loading"},{"type":"text","value":" or fetching of next or previous page"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Is the same as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFetching && !isLoading && !isFetchingNextPage && !isFetchingPreviousPage"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep in mind that imperative fetch calls, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":", may interfere with the default refetch behaviour, resulting in outdated data. Make sure to call these functions only in response to user actions, or add conditions like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasNextPage && !isFetching"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```tsx\nconst {\n  fetchNextPage,\n  fetchPreviousPage,\n  hasNextPage,\n  hasPreviousPage,\n  isFetchingNextPage,\n  isFetchingPreviousPage,\n  ...result\n} = useInfiniteQuery({\n  queryKey,\n  queryFn: ({ pageParam = 1 }) => fetchPage(pageParam),\n  ...options,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage, allPages) => lastPage.nextCursor,\n  getPreviousPageParam: (firstPage, allPages) => firstPage.prevCursor,\n})\n```\n\n**Options**\n\nThe options for `useInfiniteQuery` are identical to the [`useQuery` hook](../../../../framework/react/reference/useQuery) with the addition of the following:\n\n- `queryFn: (context: QueryFunctionContext) => Promise<TData>`\n  - **Required, but only if no default query function has been defined** [`defaultQueryFn`](../../../../framework/react/guides/default-query-function)\n  - The function that the query will use to request data.\n  - Receives a [QueryFunctionContext](../../../../framework/react/guides/query-functions#queryfunctioncontext)\n  - Must return a promise that will either resolve data or throw an error.\n  - Make sure you return the data _and_ the `pageParam` if needed for use in the props below.\n- `getNextPageParam: (lastPage, allPages) => unknown | undefined`\n  - When new data is received for this query, this function receives both the last page of the infinite list of data and the full array of all pages.\n  - It should return a **single variable** that will be passed as the last optional parameter to your query function.\n  - Return `undefined` to indicate there is no next page available.\n- `getPreviousPageParam: (firstPage, allPages) => unknown | undefined`\n  - When new data is received for this query, this function receives both the first page of the infinite list of data and the full array of all pages.\n  - It should return a **single variable** that will be passed as the last optional parameter to your query function.\n  - Return `undefined` to indicate there is no previous page available.\n\n**Returns**\n\nThe returned properties for `useInfiniteQuery` are identical to the [`useQuery` hook](../../../../framework/react/reference/useQuery), with the addition of the following and a small difference in `isRefetching`:\n\n- `data.pages: TData[]`\n  - Array containing all pages.\n- `data.pageParams: unknown[]`\n  - Array containing all page params.\n- `isFetchingNextPage: boolean`\n  - Will be `true` while fetching the next page with `fetchNextPage`.\n- `isFetchingPreviousPage: boolean`\n  - Will be `true` while fetching the previous page with `fetchPreviousPage`.\n- `fetchNextPage: (options?: FetchNextPageOptions) => Promise<UseInfiniteQueryResult>`\n  - This function allows you to fetch the next \"page\" of results.\n  - `options.pageParam: unknown` allows you to manually specify a page param instead of using `getNextPageParam`.\n  - `options.cancelRefetch: boolean` if set to `true`, calling `fetchNextPage` repeatedly will invoke `fetchPage` every time, whether the previous\n    invocation has resolved or not. Also, the result from previous invocations will be ignored. If set to `false`, calling `fetchNextPage`\n    repeatedly won't have any effect until the first invocation has resolved. Default is `true`.\n- `fetchPreviousPage: (options?: FetchPreviousPageOptions) => Promise<UseInfiniteQueryResult>`\n  - This function allows you to fetch the previous \"page\" of results.\n  - `options.pageParam: unknown` allows you to manually specify a page param instead of using `getPreviousPageParam`.\n  - `options.cancelRefetch: boolean` same as for `fetchNextPage`.\n- `hasNextPage: boolean`\n  - This will be `true` if there is a next page to be fetched (known via the `getNextPageParam` option).\n- `hasPreviousPage: boolean`\n  - This will be `true` if there is a previous page to be fetched (known via the `getPreviousPageParam` option).\n- `isRefetching: boolean`\n  - Is `true` whenever a background refetch is in-flight, which _does not_ include initial `loading` or fetching of next or previous page\n  - Is the same as `isFetching && !isLoading && !isFetchingNextPage && !isFetchingPreviousPage`\n\nKeep in mind that imperative fetch calls, such as `fetchNextPage`, may interfere with the default refetch behaviour, resulting in outdated data. Make sure to call these functions only in response to user actions, or add conditions like `hasNextPage && !isFetching`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useInfiniteQuery\ntitle: useInfiniteQuery\n---\n\n```tsx\nconst {\n  fetchNextPage,\n  fetchPreviousPage,\n  hasNextPage,\n  hasPreviousPage,\n  isFetchingNextPage,\n  isFetchingPreviousPage,\n  ...result\n} = useInfiniteQuery({\n  queryKey,\n  queryFn: ({ pageParam = 1 }) => fetchPage(pageParam),\n  ...options,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage, allPages) => lastPage.nextCursor,\n  getPreviousPageParam: (firstPage, allPages) => firstPage.prevCursor,\n})\n```\n\n**Options**\n\nThe options for `useInfiniteQuery` are identical to the [`useQuery` hook](../../../../framework/react/reference/useQuery) with the addition of the following:\n\n- `queryFn: (context: QueryFunctionContext) => Promise<TData>`\n  - **Required, but only if no default query function has been defined** [`defaultQueryFn`](../../../../framework/react/guides/default-query-function)\n  - The function that the query will use to request data.\n  - Receives a [QueryFunctionContext](../../../../framework/react/guides/query-functions#queryfunctioncontext)\n  - Must return a promise that will either resolve data or throw an error.\n  - Make sure you return the data _and_ the `pageParam` if needed for use in the props below.\n- `getNextPageParam: (lastPage, allPages) => unknown | undefined`\n  - When new data is received for this query, this function receives both the last page of the infinite list of data and the full array of all pages.\n  - It should return a **single variable** that will be passed as the last optional parameter to your query function.\n  - Return `undefined` to indicate there is no next page available.\n- `getPreviousPageParam: (firstPage, allPages) => unknown | undefined`\n  - When new data is received for this query, this function receives both the first page of the infinite list of data and the full array of all pages.\n  - It should return a **single variable** that will be passed as the last optional parameter to your query function.\n  - Return `undefined` to indicate there is no previous page available.\n\n**Returns**\n\nThe returned properties for `useInfiniteQuery` are identical to the [`useQuery` hook](../../../../framework/react/reference/useQuery), with the addition of the following and a small difference in `isRefetching`:\n\n- `data.pages: TData[]`\n  - Array containing all pages.\n- `data.pageParams: unknown[]`\n  - Array containing all page params.\n- `isFetchingNextPage: boolean`\n  - Will be `true` while fetching the next page with `fetchNextPage`.\n- `isFetchingPreviousPage: boolean`\n  - Will be `true` while fetching the previous page with `fetchPreviousPage`.\n- `fetchNextPage: (options?: FetchNextPageOptions) => Promise<UseInfiniteQueryResult>`\n  - This function allows you to fetch the next \"page\" of results.\n  - `options.pageParam: unknown` allows you to manually specify a page param instead of using `getNextPageParam`.\n  - `options.cancelRefetch: boolean` if set to `true`, calling `fetchNextPage` repeatedly will invoke `fetchPage` every time, whether the previous\n    invocation has resolved or not. Also, the result from previous invocations will be ignored. If set to `false`, calling `fetchNextPage`\n    repeatedly won't have any effect until the first invocation has resolved. Default is `true`.\n- `fetchPreviousPage: (options?: FetchPreviousPageOptions) => Promise<UseInfiniteQueryResult>`\n  - This function allows you to fetch the previous \"page\" of results.\n  - `options.pageParam: unknown` allows you to manually specify a page param instead of using `getPreviousPageParam`.\n  - `options.cancelRefetch: boolean` same as for `fetchNextPage`.\n- `hasNextPage: boolean`\n  - This will be `true` if there is a next page to be fetched (known via the `getNextPageParam` option).\n- `hasPreviousPage: boolean`\n  - This will be `true` if there is a previous page to be fetched (known via the `getPreviousPageParam` option).\n- `isRefetching: boolean`\n  - Is `true` whenever a background refetch is in-flight, which _does not_ include initial `loading` or fetching of next or previous page\n  - Is the same as `isFetching && !isLoading && !isFetchingNextPage && !isFetchingPreviousPage`\n\nKeep in mind that imperative fetch calls, such as `fetchNextPage`, may interfere with the default refetch behaviour, resulting in outdated data. Make sure to call these functions only in response to user actions, or add conditions like `hasNextPage && !isFetching`.\n"}
